3ecbbbac7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21066097?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nnnet/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nnnet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nnnet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nnnet/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nnnet","id":21066097,"login":"nnnet","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMDY2MDk3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nnnet/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nnnet/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nnnet/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nnnet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nnnet/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nnnet","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GroupHamlet/hamlet-mission-control/commits/7ba23867032607a7c02ed927e9c493eaf68b0cb5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-07T04:15:20Z","email":"zkowkmdx@sharklasers.com","name":"nnnet"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-07T04:15:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(dispatch): direct multi-provider dispatch (Anthropic / OpenAI / local OpenAI-compatible) (#648)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds a direct-dispatch path for tasks so MC no longer requires the OpenClaw gateway to reach LLMs. When the gateway isn''t available — most commonly on Linux deployments where the macOS-native gateway can''t be installed — MC now calls provider HTTP APIs itself.\n\n### Supported direct providers\n\n| Provider | Env variable | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Anthropic** | `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` | Smart Opus/Sonnet/Haiku selection via `classifyDirectModel()` heuristics. |\n| **OpenAI** | `OPENAI_API_KEY` | Models like `openai/gpt-4o-mini`, `openai/gpt-5-nano` selectable per-agent. |\n| **Any OpenAI-compatible local** | `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT`, optional `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY` | LMStudio, Ollama, vLLM — anything serving `/v1/chat/completions`. |\n\nEach agent''s `agent_config.dispatchModel` overrides the heuristics (e.g. set `openai/gpt-4o-mini` to lock that agent to OpenAI).\n\n### Hardened gateway-availability check\n\n`isGatewayAvailable()` previously returned `true` whenever `~/.openclaw` was a non-empty path string — which is the **default** even when OpenClaw isn''t installed. On Linux this caused `useDirectApi = !true && … = false`, so MC fell through to `runOpenClaw(...)` and crashed with `spawn openclaw ENOENT`.\n\nThe check now requires physical evidence:\n- A real `openclaw.json` exists at `config.openclawConfigPath`, **or**\n- A `gateways` row whose status is in `{online, healthy, ready}` (the seed `unknown` row planted by onboarding doesn''t count).\n\n## Why this is useful upstream\n\nDropping the macOS-only constraint is the single biggest barrier to running MC in cloud / Linux dev environments. With this change, an operator can `git clone`, set `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, and dispatch tasks immediately — no gateway, no Mac, no extra processes.\n\n## Walkthrough\n\n`examples/MULTI-PROVIDER-DEMO.md` is a field-by-field walkthrough that builds a three-agent team using all three direct providers (Anthropic for the lead, OpenAI for the worker, local LMStudio for the reviewer) and runs an end-to-end task.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- Run on a Linux host with no OpenClaw installed; confirm `/agents` shows \"No gateways installed\" and dispatch still works.\n- Set only `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` and dispatch a task — logs show \"Dispatching task via direct Claude API\".\n- Set only `OPENAI_API_KEY`, set agent `dispatchModel: openai/gpt-4o-mini`, dispatch — logs show OpenAI direct.\n- Bring up LMStudio at `127.0.0.1:1234`, set `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://host.docker.internal:1234/v1`, dispatch with `dispatchModel: local/<your-model>` — logs show local direct.\n- With OpenClaw running and a healthy `gateways` row, dispatch — `useDirectApi=false`, gateway path used as before. Backwards-compatible.\n\n## Provenance\n\nSquashes:\n- `70328ad feat(dispatch): direct OpenAI + OpenAI-compatible local providers`\n- `762ed51 fix(dispatch): make MC self-sufficient without OpenClaw gateway`\n- `8def310 docs(deployment): document host-config projection, direct providers, host session modes`\n- `bdd86ea docs(examples): add multi-provider team walkthrough`\n- `c7627c7 docs(examples): expand multi-provider demo into a field-by-field walkthrough`","tree":{"sha":"600bc09b83014af9f10f3ebcfa355ff559d64ea7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GroupHamlet/hamlet-mission-control/git/trees/600bc09b83014af9f10f3ebcfa355ff559d64ea7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GroupHamlet/hamlet-mission-control/git/commits/7ba23867032607a7c02ed927e9c493eaf68b0cb5","verification":{"payload":"tree 600bc09b83014af9f10f3ebcfa355ff559d64ea7\nparent b92c23a2e67789343514f5bc80aa19f6e5bb6bed\nauthor nnnet <zkowkmdx@sharklasers.com> 1778127320 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778127320 +0700\n\nfeat(dispatch): direct multi-provider dispatch (Anthropic / OpenAI / local OpenAI-compatible) (#648)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds a direct-dispatch path for tasks so MC no longer requires the OpenClaw gateway to reach LLMs. When the gateway isn''t available — most commonly on Linux deployments where the macOS-native gateway can''t be installed — MC now calls provider HTTP APIs itself.\n\n### Supported direct providers\n\n| Provider | Env variable | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Anthropic** | `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` | Smart Opus/Sonnet/Haiku selection via `classifyDirectModel()` heuristics. |\n| **OpenAI** | `OPENAI_API_KEY` | Models like `openai/gpt-4o-mini`, `openai/gpt-5-nano` selectable per-agent. |\n| **Any OpenAI-compatible local** | `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT`, optional `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY` | LMStudio, Ollama, vLLM — anything serving `/v1/chat/completions`. |\n\nEach agent''s `agent_config.dispatchModel` overrides the heuristics (e.g. set `openai/gpt-4o-mini` to lock that agent to OpenAI).\n\n### Hardened gateway-availability check\n\n`isGatewayAvailable()` previously returned `true` whenever `~/.openclaw` was a non-empty path string — which is the **default** even when OpenClaw isn''t installed. On Linux this caused `useDirectApi = !true && … = false`, so MC fell through to `runOpenClaw(...)` and crashed with `spawn openclaw ENOENT`.\n\nThe check now requires physical evidence:\n- A real `openclaw.json` exists at `config.openclawConfigPath`, **or**\n- A `gateways` row whose status is in `{online, healthy, ready}` (the seed `unknown` row planted by onboarding doesn''t count).\n\n## Why this is useful upstream\n\nDropping the macOS-only constraint is the single biggest barrier to running MC in cloud / Linux dev environments. With this change, an operator can `git clone`, set `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, and dispatch tasks immediately — no gateway, no Mac, no extra processes.\n\n## Walkthrough\n\n`examples/MULTI-PROVIDER-DEMO.md` is a field-by-field walkthrough that builds a three-agent team using all three direct providers (Anthropic for the lead, OpenAI for the worker, local LMStudio for the reviewer) and runs an end-to-end task.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- Run on a Linux host with no OpenClaw installed; confirm `/agents` shows \"No gateways installed\" and dispatch still works.\n- Set only `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` and dispatch a task — logs show \"Dispatching task via direct Claude API\".\n- Set only `OPENAI_API_KEY`, set agent `dispatchModel: openai/gpt-4o-mini`, dispatch — logs show OpenAI direct.\n- Bring up LMStudio at `127.0.0.1:1234`, set `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://host.docker.internal:1234/v1`, dispatch with `dispatchModel: local/<your-model>` — logs show local direct.\n- With OpenClaw running and a healthy `gateways` row, dispatch — `useDirectApi=false`, gateway path used as before. Backwards-compatible.\n\n## Provenance\n\nSquashes:\n- `70328ad feat(dispatch): direct OpenAI + OpenAI-compatible local providers`\n- `762ed51 fix(dispatch): make MC self-sufficient without OpenClaw gateway`\n- `8def310 docs(deployment): document host-config projection, direct providers, host session modes`\n- `bdd86ea docs(examples): add multi-provider team walkthrough`\n- `c7627c7 docs(examples): expand multi-provider demo into a field-by-field walkthrough`","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp/BHYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbB0QAGJWuiFnzKN13Dotfs3Gziqa\nSYpPll3QHlnLAAHRx9XuiRZXJDegg49xPaX41+NdJxmPIAzx8HmibjRm4nHqu178\nTpRCztankXXUUFGkmSKrr/XabeLm2Gf6DI0PWC1ymksCHK55CqvMzuxM5c/HrU0q\n6zhZQ1xsa+9G53SsUpq8ApruhvRTpSHR/lbd9OBHWHdooaau0OkjLLmGwYFfv6Ac\nx1jIHMR2lupX+JoSjpBY4csqJTn63XT9JBgqVN2ufn5zkHDvpAbI/iM+iDcjLmr2\naMYD40v70Yxks8t+C1IoWJ6sQdHKMtM3uDTVFII6EIUE6k9yfWpUhWIyTf7Tq6s9\nmDZ4M8rOSt6eTJWhNiz8NmN8HR8amqb6Xs4eFltiaWPY8McYHa9AQv7Yl8pHTwx4\ny+opflSFqTRRij2icgjwkXw6+S2BdHkWEJhG7XvzJxyDio6h1Sj4jKMIGNZ+rUTg\nPkRhvTnN6caqozd7OZSXMiU+JhWuq8gSdMVgI28nF9BPGiIfynYJsjzuCVhgaLgL\naIDSpGDsP08eXOiTRopf3hnJIYreSrpgv1N0vBzDGjHLraSGBkSKZi1Wmfmo03DV\nphTaCAmKrifg/+vjPbp9t5QmTvMVrb1pprQ7/A7RtXOFT3nQDa8VAGjE1rgcE2gY\nGNN8gaMC9kxesZBaaHX8\n=USv/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-07T17:32:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"http