"node_id":"U_kgDODZg0VA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bryannalarcon-hash/weekly-commit-module/commits/4f7cb2fe7bec1e7c7c78f8ec205b05bdd8f5a9d7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-09T15:57:57Z","email":"bryannalarcon@gmail.com","name":"bryannalarcon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-09T15:57:57Z","email":"bryannalarcon@gmail.com","name":"bryannalarcon"},"message":"Persist account profile, timezone, and notification settings\n\nThe design''s Settings → Account tab needs profile + timezone + notification\ntoggles; backend only had Outlook integration.\n\n- V10 migration: member.timezone (varchar 63) + notification_preference table\n  (5 email/digest booleans, one row per member, audit cols, unique member_id).\n- Member gains a nullable timezone; NotificationPreference entity + repo\n  mirror the OutlookPreference upsert style.\n- SettingsController: GET/PUT /api/settings/account (display name + timezone,\n  timezone validated as a real java.time.ZoneId -> 400 otherwise) and\n  GET/PUT /api/settings/notifications (lazy-defaults the 5 toggles on first\n  read). All strictly scoped to the acting member (CurrentMemberProvider,\n  never a body/path id) — Outlook integration untouched.\n\n9 ITs (SettingsControllerIT): account round-trip, invalid timezone + blank\nname rejected, notifications lazy-create + persist, cross-member isolation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d289453420f36e2d0d2718bc6e72a9ee10b081ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bryannalarcon-hash/weekly-commit-module/git/trees/d289453420f36e2d0d2718bc6e72a9ee10b081ac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bryannalarcon-hash/weekly-commit-module/git/commits/4f7cb2fe7bec1e7c7c78f8ec205b05bdd8f5a9d7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228078676?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bryannalarcon-hash","id":228078676,"login":"bryannalarcon-hash","node_id":"U_kgDODZg0VA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/bryannalarcon-hash/weekly-commit-module/commit/4f7cb2fe7bec1e7c7c78f8ec205b05bdd8f5a9d7","node_id":"C_kwDOS02XtdoAKDRmN2NiMmZlN2JlYzFlN2M3Yzc4ZjhlYzIwNWIwNWJkZDhmNWE5ZDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/bryannalarcon-hash/weekly-commit-module/commit/80b37eb191af63146b60e1111d29821561cc4c98","sha":"80b37eb191af63146b60e1111d29821561cc4c98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bryannalarcon-hash/weekly-commit-module/commits/80b37eb191af63146b60e1111d29821561cc4c98"}],"sha":"4f7cb2fe7bec1e7c7c78f8ec205b05bdd8f5a9d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bryannalarcon-hash/weekly-commit-module/commits/4f7cb2fe7bec1e7c7c78f8ec205b05bdd8f5a9d7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228078676?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bryannalarcon-hash","id":228078676,"login":"bryannalarcon-hash","node_id":"U_kgDODZg0VA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bryannalarcon-hash/weekly-commit-module/commits/80b37eb191af63146b60e1111d29821561cc4c98/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-09T15:57:56Z","email":"bryannalarcon@gmail.com","name":"bryannalarcon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-09T15:57:56Z","email":"bryannalarcon@gmail.com","name":"bryannalarcon"},"message":"Add admin RCDO edit-tree CRUD with owner fields\n\nThe new design''s Strategy screen has an admin \"Edit tree\" — add/edit/delete\nat every RCDO level. Backend was read-only, so add it:\n\n- V9 migration: nullable owner_id (FK member) on rally_cry/defining_objective/\n  outcome (+ indexes); supporting_outcome already had one. Entities gain a\n  nullable ownerId so the detail panel can show/edit an owner per node.\n- RcdoAdminController (/api/admin/rcdo) → RcdoAdminService: POST/PUT/DELETE for\n  all four levels. Create validates the parent exists (404) and the body\n  (@NotBlank title etc., 400); PUT updates title/description/window/owner and\n  never re-parents; DELETE cascades down (children first). Deleting a Supporting\n  Outcome that a commit item links is blocked 409 (existsBySupportingOutcomeId\n  guard) rather than orphaning the link.\n- Gated behind a new SCOPE_admin:rcdo authority (prod = Auth0 \"admin:rcdo\"\n  permission). E2eSecurityConfig grants it ONLY to the top-level exec\n  (managerId == null) so the hermetic demo can drive edit-tree as that admin;\n  managers/ICs still 403. GET /api/rcdo/** stays authenticated-only.\n- spotbugs-exclude: add the new admin controller/service + the (clean-build-\n  surfaced) services storing injected Spring beans, matching the existing\n  EI_EXPOSE_REP2 DI-idiom rationale.\n\n12 full-stack ITs (RcdoAdminControllerIT): CRUD per level, cascade delete,\n409 link-guard, 403 for non-admin, 404 unknown, 400 invalid.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"29774c972a2ef95370de92073d6878118ff9f689","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bryannalarcon-hash/weekly-commit-module/git/trees/29774c972a2ef95370de92073d6878118ff9f689"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bryannalarcon-hash/weekly-commit-module/git/commits/80b37eb191af63146b60e1111d29821561cc4c98","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228078676?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bryannalarcon-hash","id":228078676,"login":"bryannalarcon-hash","node_id":"U_kgDODZg0VA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/bryannalarcon-hash/weekly-commit-module/commit/80b37eb191af63146b60e1111d29821561cc4c98","node_id":"C_kwDOS02XtdoAKDgwYjM3ZWIxOTFhZjYzMTQ2YjYwZTExMTFkMjk4MjE1NjFjYzRjOTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/bryannalarcon-hash/weekly-commit-module/commit/5e85a6cc1206218ce09151618983db2b1fddee4a","sha":"5e85a6cc1206218ce09151618983db2b1fddee4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bryannalarcon-hash/weekly-commit-module/commits/5e85a6cc1206218ce09151618983db2b1fddee4a"}],"sha":"80b37eb191af63146b60e1111d29821561cc4c98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bryannalarcon-hash/weekly-commit-module/commits/80b37eb191af63146b60e1111d29821561cc4c98"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228078676?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bryannalarcon-hash","id":228078676,"login":"bryannalarcon-hash","node_id":"U_kgDODZg0VA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bryannalarcon-hash","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bryannalarcon-hash/weekly-commit-module/commits/5e85a6cc1206218ce09151618983db2b1fddee4a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-09T14:58:01Z","email":"bryannalarcon@gmail.com","name":"bryannalarcon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-09T14:58:01Z","email":"bryannalarcon@gmail.com","name":"bryannalarcon"},"message":"Tighten API contract edges (round-3 low findings)\n\nRound-3 confirmation QA found no blocking/high issues (all r2 fixes hold);\nthese are the four low contract-consistency nits it surfaced:\n\n- weekStart now parses as a STRICT ISO date (@JsonFormat yyyy-MM-dd string),\n  rejecting datetime/array/numeric encodings with 400 malformed_request so\n  the wire contract matches the OpenAPI `format: date`. (The @WeekStartBounds\n  Monday/range guard already caught any dangerous value; this just tightens\n  the accepted encodings.)\n- /error now renders RFC-7807 problem+json (ProblemErrorController) instead\n  of Boot''s whitelabel JSON, so every error surface is consistent.\n- The trailing-slash variant of /api/review-queue is now guarded by the\n  manager-scope matcher (…/review-queue/**), symmetric with /api/rollup —\n  an employee gets 403, not a 404 leaking past the matcher.\n- A non-integer @RequestParam (e.g. ?page=abc) now returns 400 with a\n  generic detail naming the parameter + type, not echoing the raw input.\n\nTests added to InputValidationIT + HttpHygieneProblemJsonIT (102 total green).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0665f81a0f00214f4f3d9558f0cad11cc035b31d"