ommits/dc4b6c458661b38c7c1b5f084d4aa2d9f1dd5032"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42197149?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vietanhrs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vietanhrs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vietanhrs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vietanhrs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vietanhrs","id":42197149,"login":"vietanhrs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyMTk3MTQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vietanhrs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vietanhrs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vietanhrs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vietanhrs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vietanhrs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vietanhrs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vietanhrs/senior-front-end-topics/commits/4ee88dc47b718be0f15e3117cd56406b3ba356ef/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-12T01:49:57Z","email":"42197149+vietanhrs@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Viet Anh Tran"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-12T01:49:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Level 10 — Modern Frontend System Architecture workbook (#17)\n\n* Add Level 10 — Modern Frontend System Architecture workbook\n\nThe capstone level: a new SPA workspace app covering 10 system-architecture\nconcepts, each with deep English theory (doc.md), an interactive in-browser\nDemo, and a fix-it Exercise with a revealable solution:\n\n- Edge rendering (TTFB-by-region sim; the data-gravity trade-off)\n- Micro-frontend orchestration (app shell + isolated, independently-loaded remotes)\n- Module Federation (live shared-scope negotiation; React-singleton or broken hooks)\n- WebAssembly integration (real hand-assembled .wasm instantiated + benchmarked)\n- IndexedDB scaling strategy (real IDB: bulk vs per-record tx, index vs full scan)\n- Server Components architecture (interactive server/client tree + bundle/boundary rules)\n- Offline-first design (real online/offline + optimistic outbox + idempotent replay)\n- Conflict resolution models (LWW/field-LWW/3-way/CRDT/manual compared on one edit)\n- Distributed UI consistency (real BroadcastChannel tabs, versioned monotonic sync)\n- Frontend system design trade-offs (constraints→architecture decision tool)\n\nWired into the workbook-hub (levels.ts + Tailwind @source), added the level 10\nentry to the shared curriculum ROADMAP (now all 10 levels complete), and updated\nroot scripts (dev:l10) and the README roadmap table/concept list/dir tree, plus a\nLevel 10 README. Full-workspace typecheck and build pass.\n\n* Fix offline-first outbox: store client id as the key so flush can delete it\n\nThe outbox enqueued with db.add(''outbox'', { type, payload }) (no id in the\nvalue, auto-generated key not captured), but flush deleted by item.id — which is\nundefined unless the store injects a keyPath. The replayed record was never\ndeleted, so the outbox would replay forever. Store the client id explicitly as\nthe outbox key (db.put with keyPath ''id'') so flush deletes the exact entry.","tree":{"sha":"a843e105128e2b01e7ea29b0894bb30eb4f4cd08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vietanhrs/senior-front-end-topics/git/trees/a843e105128e2b01e7ea29b0894bb30eb4f4cd08"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vietanhrs/senior-front-end-topics/git/commits/4ee88dc47b718be0f15e3117cd56406b3ba356ef","verification":{"payload":"tree a843e105128e2b01e7ea29b0894bb30eb4f4cd08\nparent c924e3a7adfde25f4ba5f65d547ca55c3b94994c\nauthor Viet Anh Tran <42197149+vietanhrs@users.noreply.github.com> 1781228997 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781228997 +0700\n\nLevel 10 — Modern Frontend System Architecture workbook (#17)\n\n* Add Level 10 — Modern Frontend System Architecture workbook\n\nThe capstone level: a new SPA workspace app covering 10 system-architecture\nconcepts, each with deep English theory (doc.md), an interactive in-browser\nDemo, and a fix-it Exercise with a revealable solution:\n\n- Edge rendering (TTFB-by-region sim; the data-gravity trade-off)\n- Micro-frontend orchestration (app shell + isolated, independently-loaded remotes)\n- Module Federation (live shared-scope negotiation; React-singleton or broken hooks)\n- WebAssembly integration (real hand-assembled .wasm instantiated + benchmarked)\n- IndexedDB scaling strategy (real IDB: bulk vs per-record tx, index vs full scan)\n- Server Components architecture (interactive server/client tree + bundle/boundary rules)\n- Offline-first design (real online/offline + optimistic outbox + idempotent replay)\n- Conflict resolution models (LWW/field-LWW/3-way/CRDT/manual compared on one edit)\n- Distributed UI consistency (real BroadcastChannel tabs, versioned monotonic sync)\n- Frontend system design trade-offs (constraints→architecture decision tool)\n\nWired into the workbook-hub (levels.ts + Tailwind @source), added the level 10\nentry to the shared curriculum ROADMAP (now all 10 levels complete), and updated\nroot scripts (dev:l10) and the README roadmap table/concept list/dir tree, plus a\nLevel 10 README. Full-workspace typecheck and build pass.\n\n* Fix offline-first outbox: store client id as the key so flush can delete it\n\nThe outbox enqueued with db.add(''outbox'', { type, payload }) (no id in the\nvalue, auto-generated key not captured), but flush deleted by item.id — which is\nundefined unless the store injects a keyPath. The replayed record was never\ndeleted, so the outbox would replay forever. Store the client id explicitly as\nthe outbox key (db.put with keyPath ''id'') so flush deletes the exact entry.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqK2XFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjYYQAI/SrfjOgX8XpEu/RuFh9TL