emo, and a fix-it Exercise with a revealable solution:\n\n- First Input Delay (FID) — input-delay-only metric; busy-thread inflation\n- Interaction to Next Paint (INP) — real Event Timing phase breakdown\n- Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS) — real layout-shift entries + session windows\n- Largest Contentful Paint (LCP) — buffered LCP + candidate-evolution timeline\n- PerformanceObserver API — live multi-entry-type timeline dashboard\n- Long Tasks API — real longtask entries + Total Blocking Time\n- Browser memory leak detection — controlled measurable leak + heap probe\n- Accessibility tree — live role/accessible-name (accname) + pruning\n- ARIA live regions internals — real status/alert regions + announcement model\n- Pointer events model — real pointer-capture drawing surface, coalesced events\n\nDemos drive the real browser APIs where supported (Event Timing, layout-shift,\nlargest-contentful-paint, longtask, performance.memory, pointer capture, real\naria-live regions) with feature-detected fallbacks.\n\nWired into the workbook-hub (levels.ts + Tailwind @source), added the level 9\nentry to the shared curriculum ROADMAP, and updated root scripts (dev:l9) and\nthe README roadmap/concept list/dir tree, plus a Level 9 README. Full-workspace\ntypecheck and build pass.\n\n* Address PR review on Level 9 exercises\n\n- INP exercise: correct the startTransition misconception. Its callback runs\n  synchronously, so wrapping filterAndSortHugeList() in startTransition still\n  blocks the next paint — INP stays bad. Rewrite to move the heavy compute off\n  the task (Worker, or yielded/chunked work) and route analytics through\n  sendBeacon/postTask(''background'')/requestIdleCallback instead of queueMicrotask\n  (which runs before paint). Note rAF also runs before paint.\n- performance-observer exercise: fix the flush sample that called\n  takeRecords().forEach(/* queue */) with no callback (throws TypeError at unload).\n  Keep { po, handle } per observer and drain pending entries through the same\n  handler before sendBeacon.","tree":{"sha":"a2c9cd77a9de438370a02e50c67158ac0d8c2f57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vietanhrs/senior-front-end-topics/git/trees/a2c9cd77a9de438370a02e50c67158ac0d8c2f57"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vietanhrs/senior-front-end-topics/git/commits/c924e3a7adfde25f4ba5f65d547ca55c3b94994c","verification":{"payload":"tree a2c9cd77a9de438370a02e50c67158ac0d8c2f57\nparent 0dd9f615a82042d32f38eb2ecb0e7c0bf53014e3\nauthor Viet Anh Tran <42197149+vietanhrs@users.noreply.github.com> 1781188549 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781188549 +0700\n\nLevel 9 — Performance Metrics in Practice workbook (#16)\n\n* Add Level 9 — Performance Metrics in Practice workbook\n\nNew SPA workspace app covering 10 real-world performance & UX-measurement\nconcepts, each with deep English theory (doc.md), an interactive in-browser\nDemo, and a fix-it Exercise with a revealable solution:\n\n- First Input Delay (FID) — input-delay-only metric; busy-thread inflation\n- Interaction to Next Paint (INP) — real Event Timing phase breakdown\n- Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS) — real layout-shift entries + session windows\n- Largest Contentful Paint (LCP) — buffered LCP + candidate-evolution timeline\n- PerformanceObserver API — live multi-entry-type timeline dashboard\n- Long Tasks API — real longtask entries + Total Blocking Time\n- Browser memory leak detection — controlled measurable leak + heap probe\n- Accessibility tree — live role/accessible-name (accname) + pruning\n- ARIA live regions internals — real status/alert regions + announcement model\n- Pointer events model — real pointer-capture drawing surface, coalesced events\n\nDemos drive the real browser APIs where supported (Event Timing, layout-shift,\nlargest-contentful-paint, longtask, performance.memory, pointer capture, real\naria-live regions) with feature-detected fallbacks.\n\nWired into the workbook-hub (levels.ts + Tailwind @source), added the level 9\nentry to the shared curriculum ROADMAP, and updated root scripts (dev:l9) and\nthe README roadmap/concept list/dir tree, plus a Level 9 README. Full-workspace\ntypecheck and build pass.\n\n* Address PR review on Level 9 exercises\n\n- INP exercise: correct the startTransition misconception. Its callback runs\n  synchronously, so wrapping filterAndSortHugeList() in startTransition still\n  blocks the next paint — INP stays bad. Rewrite to move the heavy compute off\n  the task (Worker, or yielded/chunked work) and route analytics through\n  sendBeacon/postTask(''background'')/requestIdleCallback instead of queueMicrotask\n  (which runs before paint). Note rAF also runs before paint.\n- performance-observer exercise: fix the flush sample that called\n  takeRecords().forEach(/* queue */) with no callback (throws TypeError at unload).\n  Keep { po, handle } per observer and drain pending entries through the same\n  handler before sendBeacon.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKsfFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAa+MQAB0D9O8dnvl2F64X23R+ZTD7\nOt4CwVcJ7JWVzBw8JNdGwl+8tppROiWY7lATaQnd6x5aLte0xR+TZhbnyUZCqLj3\nrLwLlHMd56+DCemGjyagBzBYqGwDtons5I2khV0p+KRTbqWoxfEz1bWjb2Ks15N4\nxIbNOQVF3GNFc4e0bDmMQB+0RvWaxCBpfItFhjuxPRTLZqdtY6WukdnNwpHmMYq4\nI3ENzdPcCfiHx+yp4SNoMSi4/RPq6c1pw2jRNx58Qjv/FPyol+bzIYe2EQIyHhDm\nzOIm+Jrc0GEPsFm9DN6zBtqztVy1HuVXBbnqK70kF2bhiMmCzO2M9n9Gt1mXUS/0\nFCqeJJHQhTPW2ctFcE/9hACmQHi0f4axc4oit9UZQMCNYDGNA8bR5aqxUsNJPmun\nMpCRACI1wOi5RmrkokDMyB7GxSQueBjZs28o2SE8lESMVL3DlGs/8Q6G+wxsCk6B\n0jCLhxxW9eXy/qxjLIRupqHPNhBRJqwtH6msnN0ih8OsDqaWb5OPYvxgQ2xEN8hf\nMmnna9cNT1wTTZIGTxnsnN+GCs6TsnNQGKQa+OZX8iq1D4Iip6FFXlvGyR9nNmX1\nLlVXeyumG0bnIkSD3gJyYNBgynzaJcQoSRhaFaNxGw7rcdwhslKGTrUN6LrZSUt7\ncEM1zlxKHhVSuYPeddd9\n=uFoH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-11T14:35:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vietanhrs/senior-front-end-topics/commit/c924e3a7adfde25f4ba5f65d547ca55c3b94994c","node_id":"C_kwDOS1Hb7toAKGM5MjRlM2E3YWRmZGUyNWY0YmE1ZjY1ZDU0N2NhNTVjM2I5NDk5NGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vietanhrs/senior-front-end-topics/commit/0dd9f615a82042d32f38eb2ecb0e7c0bf53014e3","sha":"0dd9f615a82042d32f38eb2ecb0e7c0bf53014e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vietanhrs/senior-front-end-topics/commits/0dd9f615a82042d32f38eb2ecb0e7c0bf53014e3"}],"sha":"c924e3a7adfde25f4ba5f65d547ca55c3b94994c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vietanhrs/senior-front-end-topics/commits/c924e3a7adfde25f4ba5f65d547ca55c3b94994c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42197149?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vietanhrs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vietanhrs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vietanhrs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vietanhrs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vietanhrs","id":42197149,"login":"vietanhrs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyMTk3MTQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vietanhrs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vietanhrs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vietanhrs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vietanhrs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vietanhrs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vietanhrs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vietanhrs/senior-front-end-topics/commits/0dd9f615a82042d32f38eb2ecb0e7c0bf53014e3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-11T11:08:23Z","email":"42197149+vietanhrs@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Viet Anh Tran"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-11T11:08:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Level 8 — Concurrency & Streams workbook (#15)\n\n* Add Level 8 — Concurrency & Streams workbook\n\nNew SPA workspace app covering 10 concurrency & streaming concepts, each with\ndeep English theory (doc.md), an interactive in-browser Demo, and a fix-it\nExercise with a revealable solution:\n\n- Task starvation (microtask flood vs yielding; heartbeat freeze)\n- Priority inversion in async code (deterministic scheduler, inheritance fix)\n- Scheduler internals (min-heap by expiration, 5ms slices, MessageChannel yield)\n- Concurrent rendering tearing (mid-render store mutation; useSyncExternalStore)\n- Backpressure handling (real Streams: push vs pull, desiredSize, bounded queues)\n- Streaming SSR pipelines (ReadableStream → TransformStream → TextEncoderStream)\n- WebRTC basics (real loopback RTCPeerConnection + DataChannel chat)\n- CRDT basics for collaboration (G-Counter convergence vs lossy LWW; OR-Set)\n- Shared memory models (SC-DRF, release/acquire publication, wait/notify)\n- Deterministic UI under async (stale-response race: latest-not-last + abort)\n\nWired into the workbook-hub (levels.ts + Tailwind @source), added the level 8\nentry to the shared curriculum ROADMAP, and updated root scripts (dev:l8) and\nthe README roadmap/concept list/dir tree, plus a Level 8 README. Full-workspace\ntypecheck and build pass.\n\n* Fix backpressure exercise: raw WebSocket has no transport backpressure\n\nThe previous solution relied on socket.pause()/resume(), which browser\nWebSocket does not have — so wrapping it in a ReadableStream gives no real\nbackpressure (onmessage keeps enqueuing past desiredSize <= 0 and the queue\ngrows unbounded).\n\nRewrite the exercise to teach the correct options:\n- WebSocketStream (Chromium): its readable read-rate governs flow → genuine\n  transport backpressure via pipeTo a slow sink\n- plain WebSocket: explicit application-level flow control — bounded buffer with\n  drop/coalesce (lossy), a server slow-down/credit message, or close+reconnect\n\nAdd a matching caveat to doc.md clarifying that backpressure only works when the\nsource can actually be paused (fetch response.body / pull() sources can; a bare\nWebSocket cannot).","tree":{"sha":"0bc76b086971781072af7f2f5d0ddb9d34e34151","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vietanhrs/senior-front-end-topics/git/trees/0bc76b086971781072af7f2f5d0ddb9d34e34151"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vietanhrs/senior-front-end-topics/git/commits/0dd9f615a82042d32f38eb2ecb0e7c0bf53014e3","verification":{"payload":"tree 0bc76b086971781072af7f2f5d0ddb9d34e34151\nparent 03676983bb78e1e9f364c135924568c6abd0dd29\nauthor Viet Anh Tran <42197149+vietanhrs@users.noreply.github.com> 1781176103 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781176103 +0700\n\nLevel 8 — Concurrency & Streams workbook (#15)\n\n* Add Level 8 — Concurrency & Streams workbook\n\nNew SPA workspace app covering 10 concurrency & streaming concepts, each with\ndeep English theory (doc.md), an interactive in-browser Demo, and a fix-it\nExercise with a revealable solution:\n\n- Task starvation (microtask flood vs yielding; heartbeat freeze)\n- Priority inversion in async code (deterministic scheduler, inheritance fix)\n- Scheduler internals (min-heap by expiration, 5ms slices, MessageChannel yield)\n- Concurrent rendering tearing (mid-render store mutation; useSyncExternalStore)\n- Backpressure handling (real Streams: push vs pull, desiredSize, bounded queues)\n- Streaming SSR pipelines (ReadableStream → TransformStream → TextEncoderStream)\n- WebRTC basics (real loopback RTCPeerConnection + DataChannel chat)\n- CRDT basics for collaboration (G-Counter convergence vs lossy LWW; OR-Set)\n- Shared memory models (SC-DRF, release/acquire publication, wait/notify)\n- Deterministic UI under async (stale-response race: latest-not-last + abort)\n\nWired into the workbook-hub (levels.ts + Tailwind @source), added the level 8\nentry to the shared curriculum ROADMAP, and updated root scripts (dev:l8) and\nthe README roadmap/concept list/dir tree, plus a Level 8 README. Full-workspace\ntypecheck and build pass.\n\n* Fix backpressure exercise: raw WebSocket has no transport backpressure\n\nThe previous solution relied on socket.pause()/resume(), which browser\nWebSocket does not have — so wrapping it in a ReadableStream gives no real\nbackpressure (onmessage keeps enqueuing past desiredSize <= 0 and the queue\ngrows unbounded).\n\nRewrite the exercise to teach the correct options:\n- WebSocketStream (Chromium): its readable read-rate governs flow → genuine\n  transport backpressure via pipeTo a slow sink\n- plain WebSocket: explicit application-level flow control — bounded buffer with\n  drop/coalesce (lossy), a server slow-down/credit message, or close+reconnect\n\nAdd a matching caveat to doc.md clarifying that backpressure only works when the\nsource can actually be paused (fetch response.body / pull() sources can; a bare\nWebSocket cannot).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKpcnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWrIQAF4P7miLKQKnPLY+ouxDjHxs\nmApU0h0Q4DgTEJSwPHEi11Vp8Us92IxJ6avjfdOgElt5/TikHmwTWvlqUkNUPLl2\nz6UfrRwo1sEs7QOSj9cuMyRTCWyCb7Ii342jrmZY+GlJ7jpcZ0JYFauqT