epos/vietanhrs/senior-front-end-topics/commits/03676983bb78e1e9f364c135924568c6abd0dd29"}],"sha":"0dd9f615a82042d32f38eb2ecb0e7c0bf53014e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vietanhrs/senior-front-end-topics/commits/0dd9f615a82042d32f38eb2ecb0e7c0bf53014e3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42197149?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vietanhrs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vietanhrs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vietanhrs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vietanhrs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vietanhrs","id":42197149,"login":"vietanhrs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyMTk3MTQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vietanhrs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vietanhrs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vietanhrs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vietanhrs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vietanhrs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vietanhrs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vietanhrs/senior-front-end-topics/commits/03676983bb78e1e9f364c135924568c6abd0dd29/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-11T03:33:14Z","email":"42197149+vietanhrs@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Viet Anh Tran"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-11T03:33:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Add level 7 concepts (#13)\n\n* Fix hub sidebar: level rows (L1, L2…) didn''t navigate\n\nThe level group used a Mantine NavLink with nested child NavLinks, so Mantine\ntreated the parent as a collapse toggle and swallowed the click — combined with a\ncontrolled `opened`, clicking a level did nothing (no navigation, no toggle).\n\nFlatten it: the level row is now a plain navigating NavLink, and its concept\nlinks render as indented siblings while that level is active. Navigation +\nauto-expand both work; single-level apps (Layout) were unaffected.\n\n* Add Level 7 — Web Platform Internals workbook\n\nNew SPA workspace app covering 10 web-platform-internals concepts, each with\ndeep English theory (doc.md), an interactive in-browser Demo, and a fix-it\nExercise with a revealable solution:\n\n- Island architecture (independent createRoot islands + JS-budget contrast)\n- Partial hydration (eager/idle/visible/interaction triggers)\n- Streaming SSR (out-of-order Suspense flush order)\n- Shadow DOM (real attachShadow, encapsulation, slots, ::part)\n- Custom elements lifecycle (live lifecycle-callback bus)\n- Web components interoperability (properties vs attributes, CustomEvent)\n- IntersectionObserver internals (thresholds, rootMargin, batched callbacks)\n- ResizeObserver loop limits (triggers the loop error, rAF-deferred fix)\n- MutationObserver cost (batched records, subtree/filter scope)\n- OffscreenCanvas (transferControlToOffscreen + off-thread worker rAF loop)\n\nWired into the workbook-hub (levels.ts + Tailwind @source), added the level 7\nentry to the shared curriculum ROADMAP, and updated root scripts (dev:l7) and\nthe README roadmap/concept list/dir tree. Full-workspace typecheck and build\npass.\n\n* Fix MutationObserver demo records\n\n* Preserve unlabelled markdown code blocks\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"db4f80dcf1f0ec193b953d80373752019fc35c8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vietanhrs/senior-front-end-topics/git/trees/db4f80dcf1f0ec193b953d80373752019fc35c8c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vietanhrs/senior-front-end-topics/git/commits/03676983bb78e1e9f364c135924568c6abd0dd29","verification":{"payload":"tree db4f80dcf1f0ec193b953d80373752019fc35c8c\nparent 5031bfa49ad1fdd545e1149c47a9bfb0572748ef\nauthor Viet Anh Tran <42197149+vietanhrs@users.noreply.github.com> 1781148794 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781148794 +0700\n\nfeat: Add level 7 concepts (#13)\n\n* Fix hub sidebar: level rows (L1, L2…) didn''t navigate\n\nThe level group used a Mantine NavLink with nested child NavLinks, so Mantine\ntreated the parent as a collapse toggle and swallowed the click — combined with a\ncontrolled `opened`, clicking a level did nothing (no navigation, no toggle).\n\nFlatten it: the level row is now a plain navigating NavLink, and its concept\nlinks render as indented siblings while that level is active. Navigation +\nauto-expand both work; single-level apps (Layout) were unaffected.\n\n* Add Level 7 — Web Platform Internals workbook\n\nNew SPA workspace app covering 10 web-platform-internals concepts, each with\ndeep English theory (doc.md), an interactive in-browser Demo, and a fix-it\nExercise with a revealable solution:\n\n- Island architecture (independent createRoot islands + JS-budget contrast)\n- Partial hydration (eager/idle/visible/interaction triggers)\n- Streaming SSR (out-of-order Suspense flush order)\n- Shadow DOM (real attachShadow, encapsulation, slots, ::part)\n- Custom elements lifecycle (live lifecycle-callback bus)\n- Web components interoperability (properties vs attributes, CustomEvent)\n- IntersectionObserver internals (thresholds, rootMargin, batched callbacks)\n- ResizeObserver loop limits (triggers the loop error, rAF-deferred fix)\n- MutationObserver cost (batched records, subtree/filter scope)\n- OffscreenCanvas (transferControlToOffscreen + off-thread worker rAF loop)\n\nWired into the workbook-hub (levels.ts + Tailwind @source), added the level 7\nentry to the shared curriculum ROADMAP, and updated root scripts (dev:l7) and\nthe README roadmap/concept list/dir tree. Full-workspace typecheck and build\npass.\n\n* Fix MutationObserver demo records\n\n* Preserve unlabelled markdown code blocks\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE---